{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/669880-vitae-blood-addiction-and-ghouls","id":669880,"title":"Vitae, Blood Addiction and Ghouls","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-18T11:01:31-07:00","id":669880,"title":"Vitae, Blood Addiction and Ghouls","content":"So I'm in a game right now and I need to IC teach a newly made ghoul PC how kindred society works and what not. Basically someone else made the ghoul and didn't do a good job so now my vamp has to baby sit it by order of the Prince.<br /> <br /> Its been a while since I've had to deal with human side of vitae so I was hoping I could run things by people here to see how my memory was.<br /> <br /> Vitae<br /> -It's addictive to humans, period.<br /> -Drinking can heal human(?)<br /> <br /> Blood Addiction<br /> -the more you drink, the more you're addicted<br /> <br /> Ghouls<br /> -made by an 'act of will'<br /> -need blood once a month to deep their powers / template<br /> -I'm a little unclear on how much of another vamp's blood they have to drink to bond to the new vamp<br /> -ghouls get a point or two of vitae to burn on healing or powers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","name":"youvegotwildtalents","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T11:18:57-07:00","id":669916,"title":"","content":"Vitae:<br /> Super addictive. The most addictive substance in the world. I believe there is a passage that says sometimes people do hard drugs ( heroine ) to try to get close to the high it gives.<br /> Drinking it can not heal a human.. unless they are a ghoul, but then they arent exactly human anymore.<br /> A vampire can bleed with blush of life, but its not vitae. So blood is not always vitae, vitae isnt exactly blood. <br /> <br /> Blood Addiction<br /> Yes this is true. Resolve composure - amount of vitae you drank<br /> <br /> Blood Bond<br /> Three stage ( i think its on pg 98?? ) one stage per night, not per drink. Humans cant resist, Vampires(supernaturals) can<br /> The blood bond Lasts a year from last drink... Give or take. So there is no overriding stage 3 bond.<br /> <br /> Ghouls:<br /> Yes. Act of will.<br /> They need to spend one point of vitae per month to stay a ghoul.<br /> They can hold 1 vitae per stamina ( so potentially they could go 5 months without needing to be hooked up )<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T12:07:04-07:00","id":669965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>youvegotwildtalents</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/669880-vitae-blood-addiction-and-ghouls#post669880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm in a game right now and I need to IC teach a newly made ghoul PC how kindred society works and what not. Basically someone else made the ghoul and didn't do a good job so now my vamp has to baby sit it by order of the Prince.<br /> <br /> Its been a while since I've had to deal with human side of vitae so I was hoping I could run things by people here to see how my memory was.<br /> <br /> Vitae<br /> -It's addictive to humans, period.<br /> -Drinking can heal human(?)<br /> <br /> Blood Addiction<br /> -the more you drink, the more you're addicted<br /> <br /> Ghouls<br /> -made by an 'act of will'<br /> -need blood once a month to deep their powers / template<br /> -I'm a little unclear on how much of another vamp's blood they have to drink to bond to the new vamp<br /> -ghouls get a point or two of vitae to burn on healing or powers</div> </div> </div> </div>Which edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T12:39:04-07:00","id":670011,"title":"","content":"Vtr 2.<br /> <br /> In terms of ghouls and blood blonds, can they resist them since they have a minor supers template? I know there are Indie ghouls who work for vitae. How do they operate without getting addicted hardcore? <br /> <br /> I know these are noob questions. I've played a fair amount of vampire but it's been awhile since I've played with a ghoul PCs and most ghouls I've encountered are NPCs/minions and there blood requirements were handed on character sheets and dot allocation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","name":"youvegotwildtalents","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:04:07-07:00","id":670054,"title":"","content":"Not as written and if allowed they would be spending a Willpower point for a chance roll to resist. It doesn't seem possible in the long term. Blood Cleansing Ritual maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T14:27:32-07:00","id":670172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/669880-vitae-blood-addiction-and-ghouls?p=670054#post670054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not as written and if allowed they would be spending a Willpower point for a chance roll to resist. It doesn't seem possible in the long term. Blood Cleansing Ritual maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. There's got to be a Dragon Ritual. Probably involves a bath tub full of kitten blood or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","name":"youvegotwildtalents","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T14:34:42-07:00","id":670177,"title":"","content":"No they can't. Greater supernatural templates can't resist vinculum either. And ghouls can't operate independently because the moment they go one month without imbibing vitae they go into withdrawal and they lose use of all their powers. If they consume vitae equal to the BP of the last vampire who fed them, their powers return. So they are under at least a partial vinculum to someone, or they're in withdrawal, which means they aren't a ghoul anymore.<br /> <br /> The up side is all stages of a vinculum disappear immediately after a year and a day passes where they haven't imbibed their regnant's blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 09-18-2015, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T14:48:04-07:00","id":670184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>youvegotwildtalents</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/669880-vitae-blood-addiction-and-ghouls?p=670172#post670172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm. There's got to be a Dragon Ritual. Probably involves a bath tub full of kitten blood or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, It's <i>called</i> &quot;Blood Cleansing Ritual&quot; and basically involves waterboarding the victim/patient. <br /> <br /> Also Ghouls go into withdrawal if they hit the monthly upkeep <i>and </i>they have no blood to spend. That's what the &quot;getting their fix&quot; line refers to. IF they have no blood they need to get more before time runs out, and IF they don't they then become deprived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T15:55:28-07:00","id":670249,"title":"","content":"edit...Found it in B&amp;S. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1031,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","user":"youvegotwildtalents","date":". 09-18-2015, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","name":"youvegotwildtalents","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T17:05:29-07:00","id":670322,"title":"","content":"A ghoul could be independent if the vampire regnant died, was in torpor, or in another city. The ghoul would need to have a 3rd level bond to that regnant though and it would only work for no more than a year. That situation might be close enough to what you were looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T17:18:28-07:00","id":670327,"title":"","content":"Actually independence is fairly easy. The willpower requirement is only necessary for the first ghouling, when one gets the template. After that you just need blood every month, which can be difficult to manage unless one is particularly cunning or knowing. We had one in our last vampire game, as a PC. It's actually kind of scary, because by the rules at least in first edition, they could manage to get all sorts of Disciplines, and while they have a small Vitae reservoir, things like the physical Disciplines don't require a Vitae use, neither do a lot of the first dot Discipline abilities.<br /> <br /> This is why, if you make a ghoul, you want them locked up in a Vinculum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T05:35:36-07:00","id":670819,"title":"","content":"Also, depending on your character, you might not *want* to tell th ghoul all of the truth. If they know all of the ins an outs of vitae and ghouldom, who's to say they won't take that knowledge, realise they've got a shit deal and bugger off? Or start poaching vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","name":"thenagain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T08:54:42-07:00","id":673235,"title":"","content":"Ghouls do not need to get vitae every month to stay a ghoul. You need to spend a vitae each month to stay a ghoul. You can hold up to your stamina, so potentially you could go 5 months without needing your infusion. Addiction fix and deprived conditions are something entirely different<br /> <br /> As far as the blood bonding goes Every template is subject to it. Humans ( which ghouls mostly are ) do not get to roll against it. All major templates, vampires, wolves, changelings, ect Do get a roll. They get to roll their BP(or equivelent) <br /> <br /> You can be fully addicted and fully functional. Think about like an alcoholic. They are addicted, they need it, they think about it, but some of them hold jobs, friends, ect and are just fine in the world. Granted it's not the best and I am not condoning it, but addicts can be fully functional people who can do their duties. So in other words your ghoul can be totally addicted to your blood and be fully capable to perform their ghouly duties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T11:11:51-07:00","id":673307,"title":"","content":"I'd allow a Ghoul to roll to resist Vibculum at a chance die. They do technically have a Blood Potency, it's just 0,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T13:16:04-07:00","id":673366,"title":"","content":"There is a ghoul merit that allows you to treat your Blood bond as one step less. I think it's a 3 dot. I allowed one of my players to make a similiar one 5 dot that treated it as 2 less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}